''Keep as burn candidates:'' L2/L8, L3, L4 (`.json` arm only), L5–L7, F6/F7, M1/M2/M5/M6/M7, E3/E4, and E5. The digest parser takes dash at `packages/lararium-mesh/src/agile-digest.ts:111-133`, while its writer emits colon at `:136-143`; tests pin dash at `packages/lararium-mesh/tests/agile-digest.test.ts:36,87`. The lifecycle reader derives missing/unknown fields at `packages/lararium-node/src/sensorium.ts:241-245`, while its builder writes the field at `:376-377`. The synced-tree `.json` probe names a retired file at `packages/lararium-node/src/synced-tree.ts:166-176`. Claude and Copilot remove old direct seats at `packages/lares-cli/src/claude-wire.ts:59-74,284` and `packages/lares-cli/src/copilot-wire.ts:57-68`.

''Keep only a wording burn:'' L1's <code>&#64;slug</code> comment at `packages/lararium-mesh/src/lar-uris.ts:370-375`; live callers pass bare roots at `packages/lararium-tw5/src/wiki-compose-handlers.ts:41` and `packages/lararium-mesh/src/genesis-doc.ts:618`. L9's earlier-shape phrase at `packages/lararium-node/src/seal-ceremony.ts:203`; the unreadable-charter refusal remains. M5's migration prose at `packages/lararium-tw5/src/types/tiddlywiki.d.ts:18-32`; current declarations need separate proof before removal.

''Drop or mark LIVE-LAW:'' F1/E1/S1 as a deletion of the no-tree census: `packages/lararium-mesh/src/sealed-writer.ts:175-188,331-346` guards occupied bytes. [wave-d] F5/E6 old-name list can burn, but retain a current unknown-file guard: `packages/lararium-node/src/vault-carriers.ts:575-587` and [wave-d] `:575-587` list old names, while [wave-d] `packages/lararium-node/src/custody-shape.ts:87-100` also refuses unknown envelopes and cleartext beside a tree. F8 stays because `packages/lararium-mesh/src/cabal-realm-clock.ts:235-236` writes both forms. M3 remains a third-party TW5 question at `packages/lararium-tw5/tests/goldens/README.md:3`. E7's bare fragment comes from the current mirror table at `packages/lararium-tw5/src/meme-normalize.ts:111-119`; keep until grammar changes. S4 is a live Nexus move at `packages/lararium-mesh/src/nexus-board-climb.ts:241-265`.

