<<~ ahu slot=`#/witness-rule`>>

!! (e) Witness rule

Extend `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs`'s corpus selector at `:127-141` to live `bags/lares/**/api/*.mem` and `bags/lararium/**/{api,mesh,browser}/*.mem`, while excluding record carriers. Match historical narration in authored comments and prose: `earlier shape`, `old shape`, `legacy`, `formerly`, `no longer`, `migration path`, `retired` when it describes the house's own previous shape. The existing `classify` logic at `:114-125` should require an exact, present-law reason for each exception. Add a structural rule for `onupgradeneeded` bodies that call `deleteObjectStore` or delete rows based on retired keys (`packages/lararium-browser/src/browser-vessel-identity.ts:94-129`). Add a producer/reader fixture for each house-owned stored grammar: the current writer output must parse, and a second house spelling must not parse (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/agile-digest.ts:111-143`). Trust-boundary malformed-input refusals stay live (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/sealed-writer.ts:175-188`).

